# Canonical author identity: thatsme <alessio.battistutta@gmail.com>
#
# History carries four variants of one person, including 166 commits whose
# author name begins with a stray UTF-8 BOM (user.name was set from BOM-encoded
# output). Matching on the commit email alone folds every name variant --
# "Alex", "<BOM>Alex", "Alessio Battistutta", "thatsme" -- into one identity,
# so the BOM never has to appear in this file.
#
# Rewriting the published history would require a force-push; this is the
# non-destructive equivalent and is applied automatically by git shortlog,
# git log, git blame, and GitHub's contributor views.

thatsme <alessio.battistutta@gmail.com> <alessio.battistutta@gmail.com>
thatsme <alessio.battistutta@gmail.com> <alessio.battistutta@hhla-plt.it>
